# Form Framework Testing Guide

## Test Form Locations

### Contact Form 7
- Admin: Plugins → Contact Form 7 → Add New
- Shortcode: `[contact-form-7 id="ID" title="Title"]`
- AJAX Events: `wpcf7mailsent`, `wpcf7submit`, `wpcf7invalid`
- DOM Success: `.wpcf7-response-output.wpcf7-mail-sent-ok`

### Gravity Forms
- Admin: Forms → New Form
- Shortcode: `[gravityform id="ID" ajax="true"]`
- JS Events: `gform_confirmation_loaded`, `gform_post_render`
- Success Indicator: `.gform_confirmation_message`

### Ninja Forms
- Admin: Ninja Forms → Add New
- Shortcode: `[ninja_form id="ID"]`
- Backbone Events: `nfRadio.channel('forms').trigger('submit:response')`
- Success: `.nf-response-msg`

### Elementor Forms
- Edit with Elementor → Add Widget → Form
- Widget ID: `elementor-form-widget-[HASH]`
- jQuery Events: `submit_success`, `form_destruct`
- Success: `.elementor-message-success`

### Avada/Fusion Forms
- Fusion Builder → Add Element → Form
- Form Class: `.fusion-form`
- AJAX Success: `.fusion-form-response-success`
- Events: Custom Fusion events

## Testing Workflow

### 1. Create Test Form
```bash
# CF7 Example
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp cf7 form add "Test CF7 Form"

# Gravity Forms Example
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp gf form create "Test GF Form"

# Ninja Forms Example
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp ninja-forms create-form --title="Test NF Form"
```

### 2. Required Fields for Choice-UFT Tracking
- Email field (type: email)
- Phone field (type: tel)
- Name field (type: text)
- Message field (type: textarea)

### 3. Verify Tracking

#### Browser Console Checks
```javascript
// Check if Choice-UFT is loaded
console.log(window.cuftUtmUtils);

// Monitor dataLayer
window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
window.dataLayer.push = function() {
    console.log('[DataLayer Push]', arguments);
    return Array.prototype.push.apply(this, arguments);
};

// Enable CUFT debugging
localStorage.setItem('cuft_debug', 'true');
```

#### Expected dataLayer Events
```javascript
{
    event: 'form_submit',
    formType: '[framework_name]',
    formId: '[form_id]',
    formName: '[form_name]',
    user_email: '[email]',
    user_phone: '[phone]',
    utm_source: '[source]',
    utm_campaign: '[campaign]',
    cuft_tracked: true
}
```

### 4. Common Issues & Solutions

#### Form Not Tracking
- Check if framework is detected: `CUFT_Form_Detector::is_framework_detected('[framework]')`
- Verify JS file loaded: Network tab → `cuft-[framework]-forms.js`
- Check for JS errors in console

#### Success State Not Detected
- Inspect DOM after submission
- Look for success classes/elements
- Check AJAX response in Network tab

#### Email/Phone Not Captured
- Verify field types are correct
- Check field names/IDs
- Ensure validation passes

## Test Scenarios

### Basic Submission Test
1. Fill all fields with valid data
2. Submit form
3. Check console for `[CUFT]` messages
4. Verify dataLayer push
5. Check MailCatcher for email

### UTM Parameter Test
1. Add UTM params to URL: `?utm_source=test&utm_campaign=test_campaign`
2. Submit form
3. Verify UTM data in dataLayer event

### Generate Lead Test
1. Ensure email + phone + click_id present
2. Submit form
3. Look for `generate_lead` event
4. Verify all required fields

### AJAX vs Standard Submission
1. Test with AJAX enabled (if supported)
2. Test with AJAX disabled
3. Compare tracking behavior

## Debug Commands

```bash
# Check plugin status
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp plugin list | grep choice-uft

# View recent form submissions in log
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress grep "form_submit" /var/www/html/wp-content/debug.log | tail -20

# Check for PHP errors
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress tail -f /var/www/html/wp-content/debug.log | grep -i error

# Monitor real-time submissions
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress tail -f /var/www/html/wp-content/debug.log | grep CUFT
```

## Validation Checklist

- [ ] Form submits successfully
- [ ] Email arrives in MailCatcher
- [ ] `form_submit` event in dataLayer
- [ ] UTM parameters captured
- [ ] Phone/email fields extracted
- [ ] No console errors
- [ ] Success message displays
- [ ] `generate_lead` fires (when applicable)

